<title>FRANCE: OECD FORECASTS FOR EU BUDGET DEFICITS.</title>
<headline>OECD FORECASTS FOR EU BUDGET DEFICITS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are tables given in the semi-annual report released by the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD) on Thursday for EU budget deficits as a percentage of gross domestic product.</p>
<p>The forecasts do not take account of any measures not yet enacted which might be taken to reduce deficits further.</p>
<p>			   1996     1997     1998</p>
<p>   Austria	     -3.9     -3.0     -3.4</p>
<p>   Belgium	     -3.4     -2.8     -2.7</p>
<p>   Denmark	     -1.6	0.0	0.7</p>
<p>   Finland	     -2.6     -2.0     -1.4</p>
<p>   France		-4.2     -3.2     -3.0</p>
<p>   Germany	     -3.8     -3.2     -2.7</p>
<p>   Greece		-7.4     -5.2     -4.0</p>
<p>   Ireland	     -0.9     -1.2     -1.0</p>
<p>   Italy		 -6.7     -3.2     -3.8</p>
<p>   Netherlands	 -2.4     -2.3     -1.7</p>
<p>   Portugal	    -4.0     -2.9     -2.8</p>
<p>   Spain		 -4.5     -3.0     -2.6</p>
<p>   Sweden		-3.6     -2.1     -0.2</p>
<p>   United Kingdom    -4.4     -2.8     -1.8</p>
<p>NOTE - The OECD gave no specific forecast for Luxembourg.</p>
</text>
